# GRIND cycle 17. Both red-first tables re-measured end to end rather than read. The
# harness is the recipe the two module docstrings record: build the plugin tree from
# git, drop in the named revision of the one script, run that module. Every row's
# "red against" revision is checked, every `guard` row is checked against every revision
# either table names, and every row naming a commit later than cfafe8e is checked at
# cfafe8e as well -- which is the claim both docstrings make about their own rows.
